---
description: Verify the HTTP implementation against its generated OpenAPI document with apidrifter
globs: ["main.py", "openapi.json", "**/routers/**", "**/routes/**", "**/api/**", "**/schemas/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When you add or change an HTTP endpoint or a Pydantic model that feeds the OpenAPI document:

1. Start the service locally (`uvicorn main:app --port 8000`). The spec is at
   http://localhost:8000/openapi.json.
2. `npx -y apidrifter plan http://localhost:8000/openapi.json --out plan.json`, then write a
   filled plan with realistic values for the slots the engine cannot infer.
3. `npx -y apidrifter run http://localhost:8000/openapi.json --base-url http://localhost:8000 --plan filled.json --format markdown`.
   http:// is only allowed for localhost. Never put real credentials in the plan or the
   command line; use `--bearer-env VAR`.
4. For each finding decide which side is the source of truth, fix that side, and rerun until
   the report is clean. Do not loosen the model to silence findings.
5. Run `python export_spec.py > openapi.json` so the committed snapshot matches, and paste
   the Markdown report into the pull request.
